                <div class="entry-body">
                    <ul>
                        <li>
                            <strong>Agentic memory runtime (GroundMem):</strong>
                            built a Neo4j-backed memory layer that validates writes as they arrive,
                            so long-running agents do not drift, mix up memories, or hallucinate
                            (LangChain/AutoGen).
                        </li>
                        <li>
                            <strong>Model Context Protocol (MCP) integration:</strong>
                            set up the servers in the runtime so agents could call tools, fetch
                            context, and talk to each other.
                        </li>
                        <li>
                            <strong>Bitemporal audit logs:</strong>
                            dual-timeline logging that lets you replay agent actions, roll back state,
                            and inspect runtime behaviour.
                        </li>
                        <li>
                            <strong>Schema &amp; rule induction:</strong>
                            built pipelines that pair LLMs with classical validation, turning
                            unstructured text into schemas, graphs, and executable rules.
                        </li>
                    </ul>
                </div>
            </div>
            <div class="entry">
                <div class="entry-meta">
                    <span class="org">CLMI-Bench</span>
                    <span class="role-line">Clinical long-horizon memory benchmark</span>
                    <span class="date">2026 to Present</span>
                </div>
                <div class="entry-body">
                    <ul>
                        <li>
                            <strong>Design:</strong>
                            two tracks. One checks block/allow medication decisions that hinge on
                            state from earlier in the episode; the other measures state fidelity
                            across episodes of 200 to 3,200 turns. Each fact becomes a family of
                            scenarios (stated, reversed, never stated, label-silent sibling, in-prompt
                            control), and a system scores only when the whole family is right. Gold
                            comes straight from FDA label contraindications.
                        </li>
                        <li>
                            <strong>Measurement:</strong>
                            every table ships with floor scores, an oracle ceiling, and a full-context
                            control. Results carry cluster-bootstrap intervals and exact paired tests
                            with Holm correction, and test labels stay withheld under a published hash.
                        </li>
                    </ul>
                </div>
            </div>
